      "writtenOn": "2018-03-20T05:54:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027enroll_session\u0027 is behaving as if it were \u0027previous_sensor_mode\u0027 but just with the FP_MODE_ENROLL_SESSION bit (for easier maintenance only, we could keep all the bits).\nThe idea behind it is that there is a lot of \u0027state\u0027 in the enrollment (particularly in the private algorithm library) so we need to detect when the host transition the ENROLL_SESSION bit to do inits/clean-up, so it is used to compare the previous state to the new state set by the host in sensor_mode.\nSuggestions for a better comment wording are also welcome",
      "parentUuid": "456f1180_34040aa2",
